  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ankit Sharma vs Nyaynirday Adhikari Khady Suraksha ... on 21 November, 2025 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Gwl:30976 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice G. S. Ahluwalia On The 21st Of November, 2025 Miscellaneous Second Appeal No. 28 of 2025 Ankit Sharma And Others Versus Nyaynirday Adhikari Khady Suraksha Karyalay Ohadpur And Others Appearance: Shri Pramod Kumar Gohadkar, Advocate for the applican Shri S.S. Kushwaha, Government Advocate for responden Judgment",
    "facts": "This miscellaneous second appeal, under section 71(6) Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"the FSSA\") has been filed against the order dated 5/3/2025 passed by IX District Judge, Gwalior in RCA No. 6/2025, as well as, order dated 28/10/2024 passed by Adjudicating Officer/Additional District Magistrate, Gwalior in case No. Q/Food safety/12/2022. 2. Facts necessary for disposal of present appeal, in short, are that complainant filed a complaint before the Adjudicating Officer alleging inter alia that on 23/10/2021, at about 11:35 a.m., FSO inspected the dairy where appellant was present and he informed that owner of dairy is his father Munnalal Sharma. It was found that 30 kg of Paneer, 20 kg of curd, 12 kg of ghee and 35 liters of milk-mix were stored and were meant for sale. Since the FSO had a suspicion that the aforesaid articles might be substandard, therefore samples were collected. As per the report of the Food Analyst, the Paneer was found to be of substandard NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-GWL:30976 2 MSA-28-2025 quality. Copy of report was sent to the appellant with an information that he can file an appeal under section 46(4) of FSSA and under 2.4.2(6) of Food Safety and Standard Rules, 2011. However, appellant did not prefer any appeal.",
    "arguments": "5. A solitary ground has been raised by counsel for appellant that penalty amount may be further reduced. 6. Sale of substandard food articles is detrimental to the mankind.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. A solitary ground has been raised by counsel for appellant that penalty amount may be further reduced. 6. Sale of substandard food articles is detrimental to the mankind.",
